{
  "_readme": "Repo-shared Claude Code settings for mimicwarehouse (decision D-39 + EP-165/D-43; GOVERNANCE.md section 4). Four parts: (1) deny rules that keep Claude sessions from reading licensed patient-level data (PhysioNet Credentialed Health Data License 1.5.0) via the Read/Grep/Glob tools, shell readers, two-step copy/interpreter paths (cp, python -c, uv run python, nested sh -c, .NET file APIs), or the duckdb executable, plus the send/write tools of claude.ai MCP connectors (reference lookups only, GOVERNANCE section 4); (2) allow rules for read-only project commands (convenience only — deny rules keep precedence and cannot be overridden by settings.local.json); (3) env PYTHONUTF8=1 so both tool shells run Python with UTF-8 stdio (Risk 13); (4) a PreToolUse command-string hook (mimicwarehouse/scripts/claude_pretool_guard.py, run by the allow-listed workspace venv python — path-bound like the pre-commit hook, re-wire after moving the clone) that denies any command/path mentioning mimicdata / source material / .csv / .parquet / .duckdb unless it is an allow-listed project launcher. The deny list is a blocklist of common forms, not a data-path firewall — the hook, CLAUDE.md prose and safe_query (EP-30) are the remaining layers. All data access goes through mimicwarehouse.safe.safe_query / `mwh sql` (read-only, k=11 suppression, audit-logged). Do not weaken without updating GOVERNANCE.md and DECISIONS.md; `mwh guard --selfcheck` pins the hook registration.",
